es of the slope field become horizontal as $y\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\n- The slopes of the slope field are negative for $y\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (2,\\infty )$ and positive for $y\\in (-2,2).$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{4-{y}^{2}}$ gives the required behavior. Notice that ${y}^{′}\\to 0$ as $y\\to \\infty ,$ and ${y}^{′}\\to \\infty $ as $y\\to \\pm 2.$ Also, the right-hand side of this equation is negative for $y\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (2,\\infty )$ and  positive for $y\\in (-2,2).$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4-{y}^{2}}$ does *not* give the required behavior. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4-{y}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{(\\frac{4}{{y}^{2}}-1)}\\to -1\\,\\text{as}\\,y\\to \\pm \\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slopes of the slope field for this differential equation do not become horizontal as $y\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}-4}$ does *not* give the required behavior. The slopes of the slope field for this differential equation are negative for $y\\in (-2,2)$ and positive for $y\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (2,\\infty ).$" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312231 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312232 13194139534820 true] [17592186312231 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312233 13194139534820 true] [17592186312231 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312234 13194139534820 true] [17592186312231 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312235 13194139534820 true] [17592186312231 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312236 13194139534820 true] [17592186312231 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534820 true] [17592186312231 1041 "selection" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312231 1104 #edb/ref 17592186312233 13194139534820 true] [17592186312231 1110 #uuid "bbb1feca-29c3-579f-8d6c-bee8c2363c6e" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312232 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312232 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534820 true] [17592186312232 1111 #uuid "9eb8be23-8455-52ab-868c-75a3ec81a649" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312233 1034 "I o