d, let's consider each equation.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{y+3}$ gives the required behavior. Notice that ${y}^{′}\\to 0$ as $y\\to \\infty ,$ and ${y}^{′}\\to \\infty $ as $y\\to -3.$ Also, the right-hand side of this equation is positive for $y<-3$ and negative for $y>-3.$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{(y+3)^{2}}$ does *not* give the required behavior. The slopes of the slope field for this differential equation are positive for all $y\\ne -3.$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{y}{y+3}$ does *not* give the required behavior. Notice that\n\n$$\n-\\frac{y}{y+3}=-\\frac{1}{(1+\\frac{3}{y})}\\to -1\\,\\text{as}\\,y\\to \\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slopes of the slope field for this differential equation do not become horizontal as $y\\to \\infty .$" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312238 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312239 13194139534820 true] [17592186312238 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312240 13194139534820 true] [17592186312238 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312241 13194139534820 true] [17592186312238 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312242 13194139534820 true] [17592186312238 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312243 13194139534820 true] [17592186312238 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534820 true] [17592186312238 1041 "selection" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312238 1104 #edb/ref 17592186312240 13194139534820 true] [17592186312238 1110 #uuid "a5c0ae67-1820-5b19-9dae-454cd1c16ee4" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312239 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312239 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534820 true] [17592186312239 1111 #uuid "a1aa5239-8a35-5cd1-99ef-772d9e0a00f7" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312240 1034 "I only" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312240 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534820 true] [17592186312240 1111 #uuid "1e2520e5-bba1-591b-8b1e-d69400ed3874" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312241 1034 "III only" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312241 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534820 true] [17592186312241 1111 #uuid "3f210340-3870-54dc-94c5-5a0a29010007" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312242 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312242 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534820 true] [17592186312242 1111 #uuid "6dd18036-320b-5082-8f0f-9077e89d3c70" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312243 1034 "II only" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312243 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534820 true] [17592186312243 1111 #uuid "9479bf72-de58-51a0-af9c-b6beed775887" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312244 1017 #edb/ref 17592186312245 13194139534820 true] [17592186312244 1089 "q-116150" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312244 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534820 true] [17592186312244 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040443/assets/158e4f6067ce12d5a31cc6ee0b217a8d11a459db5883fdd0b28ffdc2bd969a5e.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=-{y}^{3}-2{y}^{2}$\n- ${y}^{′}={y}^{3}+4{y}^{2}+4y$\n- ${y}^{′}=2y-{y}^{2}$" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312244 1113 #uuid "31f2f4de-cad5-594e-ac30-aec769441ed5" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312244 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040443/assets/41b6dc7fd4e9a7dba6e14fe2d9fb87e7c07736ec0fc3cc111dd347b61c1075bb.png)\n\n \n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slope field is zero along the lines $y=-2$ and $y=0.$ Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\n- Second, the lines $y=-2$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into $3$ regions. The sign of the slopes in each of the $3$ regions are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| Region | $y<-2$ | $-2<y<0$ | $y>0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↗$ | $↘$ | $↘$ |\n| Sign | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-{y}^{3}-2{y}^{2}=-{y}^{2}(y+2)\n$$\n\ngives the required behavior.\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={y}^{3}+4{y}^{2}+4y=y({y}^{2}+4y+4)=y(y+2)^{2}\n$$\n\ndoes *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $y=-2$ and $y=0,$ but the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) do not correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| Region | $y<-2$ | $-2<y<0$ | $y>0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↘$ | $↘$ | $↗$ |\n| Sign | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2y-{y}^{2}=y(2-y)\n$$\n\ndoes *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $y=0$ and $y=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312245 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312246 13194139534820 true] [17592186312245 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312247 13194139534820 true] [17592186312245 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312248 13194139534820 true] [17592186312245 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312249 13194139534820 true] [17592186312245 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312250 13194139534820 true] [17592186312245 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534820 true] [17592186312245 1041 "selection" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312245 1104 #edb/ref 17592186312248 13194139534820 true] [17592186312245 1110 #uuid "d04f0e4c-7667-5285-85f6-c703117462b2" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312246 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312246 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534820 true] [17592186312246 1111 #uuid "e01615d7-3f77-5bc5-aa72-53fea87fc2a5" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312247 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312247 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534820 true] [17592186312247 1111 #uuid "53bd281b-bf8c-5d65-9736-ebf364853ef9" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312248 1034 "I only" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312248 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534820 true] [17592186312248 1111 #uuid "7cd80012-7dc7-589b-a7aa-db23a84a638f" 13194139534820 t