$ | $↘$ |\n| Sign | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n\nOf the two remaining options, the only one that gives this behavior is\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-{y}^{3}+6{y}^{2}-9y=-y(y-3)^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}=-{y}^{3}+6{y}^{2}-9y.$" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312252 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312253 13194139534820 true] [17592186312252 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312254 13194139534820 true] [17592186312252 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312255 13194139534820 true] [17592186312252 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312256 13194139534820 true] [17592186312252 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312257 13194139534820 true] [17592186312252 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534820 true] [17592186312252 1041 "selection" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312252 1104 #edb/ref 17592186312253 13194139534820 true] [17592186312252 1110 #uuid "7572c058-ad5a-5f9d-ad76-fe2d14b72320" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312253 1034 "{y}^{′}=-{y}^{3}+6{y}^{2}-9y" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312253 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534820 true] [17592186312253 1111 #uuid "4c25163c-f30b-5e16-88c0-91b7e09eb3f1" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312254 1034 "{y}^{′}={y}^{2}-3y" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312254 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534820 true] [17592186312254 1111 #uuid "60bc6cbb-a2ef-516a-8ca2-6ccd95cb5c08" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312255 1034 "{y}^{′}={y}^{3}-{y}^{2}" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312255 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534820 true] [17592186312255 1111 #uuid "11b57f26-8990-5ca2-9cc0-995ccf3e08ea" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312256 1034 "{y}^{′}=3{y}^{3}" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312256 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534820 true] [17592186312256 1111 #uuid "7d6a98f0-ff1a-549c-bdc8-ba332d0a0a7e" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312257 1034 "{y}^{′}=3y-{y}^{3}" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312257 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534820 true] [17592186312257 1111 #uuid "7c953b27-c5e7-5fcc-897c-388b13d33867" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312258 1017 #edb/ref 17592186312259 13194139534820 true] [17592186312258 1089 "q-116177" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312258 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534820 true] [17592186312258 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040443/assets/8f023d50d11e5b6604e5fcc257e35aa4b8615e8c91f5855d10e73293720c27e4.png)\n\nIdentify the differential equation that generated the slope field above." 13194139534820 true] [17592186312258 1113 #uuid "d0cf6ca5-4b24-52a6-9510-ae0b22a2d68e" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312258 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040443/assets/b6cf036f732d1cdff6f2e575b2ce082979d986416afd195282789303dcf70131.png)\n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slopes become vertical as $y\\to \\pm 1.$\n\nOf the given equations, the only equations that satisfy this condition are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{(y+1)(y-1)^{2}} \\\\ {y}^{′} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{y}^{2}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Second, the slopes become horizontal as $y\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\nOf the remaining options, the only one that gives this behavior is\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{(y+1)(y-1)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{(y+1)(y-1)^{2}}\\to 0\\,\\text{as}\\,y\\to \\pm \\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slopes of the slope field for the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{(y+1)(y-1)^{2}}$ become horizontal as $y\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{y}^{2}-1}=\\frac{1}{(1-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}})}\\to 1\\,\\text{as}\\,y\\to \\pm \\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slopes of the slope field for the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{y}^{2}-1}$ do *not* become horizontal as $y\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\nSo, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{(y+1)(y-1)^{2}}.$" 13194139534820 true] [17592186312259 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312260 13194139534820 true] [17592186312259 1000 #edb/ref 175921